主要终点:
Modified Ashworth Scale (MAS) score

\*\*The Modified Ashworth Scale (MAS)\*\* is a 6-point categorical scale that measures resistance during passive muscle stretching. It is scored as follows: 0 = No increase in muscle tone;

1 = Slight increase in muscle tone, manifested by a catch and release or by minimal resistance at the end of the range of motion;

1+ = Slight increase in muscle tone, manifested by a catch, followed by minimal resistance throughout less than half of the remainder of the range of motion; 2 = More marked increase in muscle tone through most of the range of motion, but the affected part(s) are easily moved; 3 = Considerable increase in muscle tone, making passive movement difficult; 4 = Affected part(s) rigid in flexion or extension.

Change in Modified Ashworth Scale (MAS) score from baseline to Week 5.

